# The guess that `texts` is a list was opened for `length` and the difference alone: a read by key off a list that a test has proven has a form that still asks the list for its storage, and such a form counted for nothing outside loops.
# So the arms met in front of the reads, `texts` was anything again, and each read called the stub that asks what it reads off. The reads count: the arms meet behind them: two reads off a proven list in the typed run, two closed ones in the arm.
# (`ends` may have a guard at its entry, which proves the list for the whole body: it is there for its answers.)
# RUN(READS): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# READS-COUNT-2: = GetArrayElement {{*}} arrayStorage=Contiguous level=Expected
# RUN(CLOSED): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CLOSED-COUNT-2: = ElemGet
# A call between the length and the reads ends the stretch as ever.
# RUN(CALL): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CALL-NOT: = ElemGet
# Lists of every storage, with holes, sparse, frozen, of a class below with an accessor; a text, bytes, records like lists, arguments, a proxy, nothing.
